---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";

const constraints = [
  ["Keep", "Every original future game in its assigned week"],
  ["Prefer", "Open slots created by games that were played early"],
  ["Balance", "Added make-up games across the remaining weeks"],
  ["Limit", "Normally no more than three matches per player per night"],
  ["Avoid", "The same two players meeting twice in one future night"],
  ["Reject", "Any plan missing a game or one of the required pairings"],
];
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Dart League Schedule & Standings"
  description="A personal Python project built around a real darts-league problem, showing how I turn scheduling constraints and published results into reliable, auditable schedules and reports."
  eyebrow="Python automation · Constraint logic"
  emoji="🎯"
  repo="https://github.com/GlassHouse97/Darts-League-Schedule"
  accent="#ff8f80"
>
  <div slot="hero-visual" class="schedule-stack">
    <div class="sheet sheet-back"></div>
    <div class="sheet sheet-front">
      <img src="/assets/darts/darts-schedule.png" alt="Generated Long Island Elite PDSL standings and results schedule" width="1224" height="1584" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div slot="stats" class="stat"><strong>30</strong><span>Games per division</span></div>
  <div slot="stats" class="stat"><strong>15</strong><span>Unique pairings</span></div>
  <div slot="stats" class="stat"><strong>2×</strong><span>Each pairing repeats</span></div>
  <div slot="stats" class="stat"><strong>PDF</strong><span>Auditable output</span></div>

  <section class="project-section">
    <div><span class="section-number">01</span><h2>The oddly specific problem</h2></div>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p>League matches do not always happen in the neat order printed on the original schedule. Games are played early, postponed, or completed as late make-ups, and the remaining plan still has to be fair.</p>
      <p>
        This tool keeps the fixed seat-number grid separate from player names, matches published DartConnect recaps back to the canonical schedule, and labels each original slot as played, early, late make-up, incomplete, or still to play.
      </p>
      <div class="callout"><strong>The practical goal.</strong> Make the rest of the season easier to run without losing the audit trail back to the original 30-game plan.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="project-section">
    <div><span class="section-number">02</span><h2>The planning logic</h2></div>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p>The solver is not simply filling the next empty row. It is balancing player load, future weeks, repeat matchups, and the integrity of the original schedule.</p>
      <div class="constraint-list">
        {constraints.map(([verb, detail], index) => (
          <div>
            <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
            <strong>{verb}</strong>
            <p>{detail}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="project-section">
    <div><span class="section-number">03</span><h2>From browser recap to finished schedule</h2></div>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p>Published match data becomes a stable local ledger, then an auditable plan and a report people can actually use on league night.</p>
      <ol class="flow-list">
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Refresh</strong><p>Optionally collect JavaScript-rendered DartConnect results and standings with Playwright.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Reconcile</strong><p>Map the recap order back to the canonical game number and preserve actual week and slot separately.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Plan</strong><p>Find placements for incomplete games while respecting player and pairing constraints.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Validate</strong><p>Reject the plan unless all 30 games and all 15 twice-played pairings are accounted for.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>05</span><div><strong>Publish</strong><p>Generate standings, results, future schedules, make-up notes, and a JSON audit summary.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="project-section">
    <div><span class="section-number">04</span><h2>The output</h2></div>
    <div class="body-copy output-grid">
      <figure>
        <img src="/assets/darts/darts-scheduling-illustration.png" alt="Stylized dartboard and scheduling grid representing the league planning problem" width="1536" height="1024" />
        <figcaption>A stylized view of the scheduling problem rather than a distorted document preview.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
      <p>The PDF is meant for everyday use. The accompanying JSON summary is meant for auditing and later edits.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Readable division standings</li>
          <li>Actual results grouped by played week</li>
          <li>Future schedule with make-up placements</li>
          <li>Notes showing original week and open-slot use</li>
          <li>Player loads and inferred seat mapping</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="project-section">
    <div><span class="section-number">05</span><h2>Why this project matters</h2></div>
    <div class="body-copy">
      <p>This was another personal project built around a problem I actually needed to solve. It gave me a practical way to demonstrate how I turn real-world rules, imperfect inputs, and edge cases into software people can trust.</p>
      <p>
        The interesting part is not simply generating a PDF. It is separating stable identities from presentation names, preserving original and actual schedule positions, expressing human constraints clearly, and refusing to publish an invalid result.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row project-buttons">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/GlassHouse97/Darts-League-Schedule" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the scheduling tool <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>

<style>
  .schedule-stack {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 570px;
  }

  .sheet {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: min(76%, 390px);
    aspect-ratio: 8.5 / 11;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: white;
    box-shadow: 0 32px 90px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.48);
  }

  .sheet-back {
    opacity: 0.38;
    transform: translate(-55%, -48%) rotate(-8deg);
  }

  .sheet-front {
    overflow: hidden;
    transform: translate(-45%, -50%) rotate(4deg);
  }

  .sheet-front img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: top;
  }

  .constraint-list {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .constraint-list > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 42px 90px 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-block: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .constraint-list span {
    color: var(--coral);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
  }

  .constraint-list strong {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .constraint-list p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .flow-list {
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .flow-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 48px 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 0;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
  }

  .flow-list li:first-child {
    border-radius: 14px 14px 0 0;
  }

  .flow-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 0 0 14px 14px;
  }

  .flow-list li > span {
    color: var(--coral);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }

  .flow-list strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .flow-list p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .output-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(300px, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: center;
    max-width: none !important;
  }

  figure {
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: var(--night-soft);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  figure img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  figcaption {
    padding: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.025);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .project-buttons {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .schedule-stack {
      min-height: 470px;
    }

    .output-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    figure {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 520px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .constraint-list > div {
      grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr;
    }

    .constraint-list p {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
